Now we have a working code that can do HD with TG forcing, null initial conditions.
To run:

* GHOST/3D/src/examples/parameter.inp has a working input file.
* To compile, do:
  cd GHOST/3D/build
  cmake .. -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/path/to/your/mpi -DFFTW3_ROOT=/path/to/your/fftw
  make

Things to discuss:

INITIAL CONDITIONS AND FORCING:
* The initial condition (IC) factory now allows us to set only one IC. It's ready
(but the lists are commented out) to loop through a list of ICs and apply them as
an operator. The same should be done for the forcing. This is relatively 
straightforward.

* The forcing factory needs two methods: one to set up the forcing, one to update.
What we have can work but we must find a way to reuse the update to multiple 
initial forcings.

GSTATES:
* The GState now is complex by default, as all our field states are complex. 
However, for the forcing some solvers need a mix of complex and real arrays. Maybe 
the forcing should be a different type?

* The IC and forcing classes are not aware of the structure of the GStates (e.g.,
they don't have access to the field mask (solver%VELOCITY, solver%SCALAR, etc.). 
Should this mask be defined by the IC and be a property of GState instead of by 
the solver? This can simplify some things (right now we have to pass the solver 
class to the IC and forcing factories), but may affect other choices.

PARTICLES:
* Should particles be initialized and evolved in "main", or by each solver? The
former choice allows us to do "active" particles in the future (now we can, as we
do in the PIC solver, but it is not optimal). 
